detalheSolucao.en:
I developed a Python tool capable of automatically interpreting Individualized BPA (BPAI) and Consolidated BPA (BPAC) production reports:
- Validates and processes only if the input files have the actual format and content of both BPAI and BPAC reports;
- Identifies CNES, procedures, and quantities;
- Consolidates productions by CNES → procedure → quantity;
- Concatenates each record into a single String, filling the required positions with default values and characters that must occupy a fixed position in the line;
- Allows the user to input a specific competence month for that file in YYYYMM format (YYYY = Year; MM = Month), removing the need to update the system for each new competence month;
- Automatically generates the file in the layout required by the Magnetic FPO;
- Has a graphical interface built with TKinter, with usage instructions, to facilitate its use by non-technical users.

Besides the processing logic, the project involved analyzing the FPO import layout and reverse-engineering files generated by the federal systems themselves.

detalheResultado.en:
▶ The process went from approximately 5 hours to about 5 minutes, considering everything from obtaining the reports in the BPA to importing the generated file into the FPO;
▶ An approximate 98% reduction in execution time, eliminating the need for manual typing of quantities and completely eliminating the possibility of human errors;
▶ Zero rejections and inconsistencies when comparing the Presented Value vs. Approved Value.

