▶ Solid foundation for integration into customer experience (CX) analysis pipelines, leaning more towards the commercial sphere, since there is a great difficulty for the model to identify sarcasm, irony, and/or double meaning, as it is a much more human condition, difficult for a machine to understand.

detalheSolucao.en:
An interactive Python system that analyzes and weights relationships between movies through three fundamental criteria:
- Genre: Identification of titles with the same thematic category;
- Cast: Mapping of main actors intersection;
- Duration: Grouping of movies with a runtime variation of up to 30 minutes;

Based on the logical expression R = G ∨ A ∨ D, the tool consolidates the connections into adjacency matrices (binary and by similarity weight) and generates representations in graphs using Spring Layout. All interaction is performed through a graphical interface in Tkinter.

detalheResultado.en:
▶ Demonstration and practical application of discrete structures in recommendation systems;
▶ Similarity mapping with dynamic adjacency matrices and interactive graphs generated via NetworkX and Matplotlib;
▶ User-friendly graphical interface developed in Tkinter to easily switch between individual criteria analysis or weighted overview.

detalheSolucao.en:
